          "path": "_m/g/c/p/v/newington-green-unitarian-church-wp/church-walk-geograph-org-uk-15.jpg",
          "filename": "Church Walk - geograph.org.uk - 1598324.jpg",
          "caption": "Church Walk This was the old path running between Newington Green and Stoke Newington, from the Dissenters' chapel (Newington Green Unitarian Church, the main building on the left) to the centre of the parish, St Mary's (Old) Church. It very roughly parallels Green Lanes, and in the days when that was a drovers' road, would have provided a quieter and less muddy walk between the villages. \nEasily overlooked, it now threads between shabby houses and back gardens but still retains a rustic character in its winding route.",
          "alt": "Church Walk This was the old path running between Newington Green and Stoke Newington, from the Dissenters' chapel (Newington Green Unitarian Church, the main building on the left) to the centre of the parish, St Mary's (Old) Church. It very roughly parallels Green Lanes, and in the days when that was a drovers' road, would have provided a quieter and less muddy walk between the villages. \nEasily overlooked, it now threads between shabby houses and back gardens but still retains a rustic character in its winding route.",
